hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of Marlena masters I  believe that the fastest and most  effective way to grow a business is some  model the strategies of people who've  already done what you're trying to do so  today we're gonna look at how a young  boy who grew up with a single mother and  was contemplating suicide in his early  years turn his life around by starting  his own business and went on to become  worth over five hundred million dollars  today this is a story of celebrity chef  entrepreneur Wolfgang Puck and the top  three lessons you can learn from his  success Wolfgang Puck was born to a  hotel chef mother and a butcher father  the art and love of preparing food was  in his blood Huck's father abandoned his  mother just before his birth leaving  Maria as a single mother in 1956 she  remarried the coal miner Joseph puck  with an adopted Wolfgang making him  Wolfgang Puck this marriage will result  in two younger sisters and their little  brother for puck under the guidance of  his mother who'd been dabbling in the  professional culinary arts for some time  puck began cooking pastries he had made  up his mind and an early age that he  wanted to follow in his mother's  footsteps and become a professional chef  instead of following the traditional  route of first attending culinary school  Puck chose to instead train under an  apprenticeship from the age of 14 he was  sent on a train to southern Austria to  work in a hotel kitchen but did not find  success he had hoped for after stepping  out the cakes on a bakery floor he  recalls that everyone told me I'm good  for nothing  a few days later the head chef told puck  you better go home to your mother's she  can breastfeed you for another year  after pondering suicide puck chose  instead to apprentice at another hotel  it proved to be a wise decision  puck decided to move to the United  States in 1973 and worked in several  restaurants before finding a home at  mommy's own failing a Hollywood  restaurant there he would bring the  restaurant back to prominence and become  co-owner  in 1982 PUC launched his first cookbook  modern French cooking for the American  kitchen with the success that followed  and upon meeting his future wife and  business partner  Barbara Lazarov who would encourage him  to follow his dreams PUC got the  confidence he needed to finally realize  one of his lifelong goals PUC was going  to open his own restaurant with the  backing of some investors he opened  Spago and the rest is history by  sticking with his passion am I not  letting people get him down Wolfgang  Puck was able to go from someone  committing suicide to becoming one of  the most well-known celebrity  entrepreneurships in the world to help  you take the next step  here are three action items you can  learn from Wolfgang Puck action item  number one don't complicate things the  easier it is for someone to understand  what it is that you do the easier it's  gonna be for them to sign up as a  customer and tell their friends about  you keep things simple focus on the  highest value that you can bring your  clients and be the best in the world at  what you do  the longer takes prospects to understand  your message the harder it's going to be  to grow your business PUC has never been  one for pretensions despite being a  gourmet chef who caters to the who's who  of Hollywood  I'm Amy of America's other elite PUC has  refused to succumb to the glitz and the  airs of many of the other top chefs he's  kept his recipes simple and their  presentation equally so as restaurants  designs unfussy and his overall message  clear-cut don't make it complicated  indeed for over 25 years people have  kept coming back and telling their  friends it's a casual yet sophisticated  nature with which PUC approaches all of  his businesses that has endeared him to  the American public as well as his  culinary peers his priority has always  been on creating simple innovative and  tasty food and to share that with as  many people as possible everything  beyond the food is an afterthought  according to Puck I think people can  walk by and they see the menu it's not  intimidating and the food is interesting  if they get good food friendly service  in a nice environment people will come  back and tell their friends it is the  happy customer who makes the ambience of  the restaurant inviting and excited  so I always believe great food great  service and wonderful customers put into  the right space will make a successful  restaurant if you buy good food fresh  green beans you don't have to line them  up in a row or anything like that  just put them out on a nice-looking  plate a mixture of things they are  familiar with and new things to auction  item number two hire good people  you'll always be limited in your growth  until you start bringing on people to  help you you only have so much time with  the day surround yourself with people  who complement your weaknesses and who  you can trust  hire slowly after doing a lot of legwork  and fire quickly if it's not a good fit  the better people you hire the more your  company will grow it's a simple design  despite being the name behind the brand  as well as its main inspiration and  talent the road to success is not one  that puck has walked alone from his  early days before the first bog was even  launched puck had the foresight to  surround himself by only the most  qualified and only those who he knew he  could trust as the company continued to  grow at an astonishing rate puck would  replace his business partners and  management staff as necessary choosing a  place in control those who are most  qualified to be there and who had the  kind of experience that he desired he  always believed that you had the higher  talent to create a successful business  according to puck whether you have one  restaurant or 10 or 20 or more the most  important thing is to hire good people  when they need me I go if they don't  need me as much I don't go as much we're  much better organized and we have much  better management what we have that a  lot of other caterers don't is a lot of  talent and chefs I'm not saying that  nobody else has talented people but  nobody has as many as we have action  atom number three never give up as an  entrepreneur you're gonna face some dark  times you'll think about giving up I'm  gonna work for someone else don't lose  hope don't give up on your dream do  something every day that will move you  closer to your end goal and don't let  anything else get in your way eventually  you will know success  it would appear puck is always  successful but the path to success was  not as smooth that it might appear he  stumbled numerous times along the way  and often had to learn things the hard  way  but he never failed to pick himself up  and get right back to work it was in  this recovery process the puck often  learned some of the most important  business lessons that he would use later  on in his career the closures and losses  were not easy for puck especially in the  early days when he was first starting  out and each new venture was close to  life or death but with each failure came  a lesson according the puck each time  something went wrong each time you made  a mistake that was one less mistake that  he would ever make again in the future  weather was to do with budgeting issues  management promotions or the food itself  puck made use of every opportunity to  learn what he could in order to avoid  similar problems in the future  according to puck I learned more from  the one restaurant that didn't work than  from all the ones that were successes  only you can judge your life you have to  live up to your own expectations there  is no value with just one restaurant or  with one person the brand has to be  bigger than the person  so remember don't complicate things hire  good people and never give up to finish  up this video I wanted to share one of  my favorite true stories about Wolfgang  Puck and some of his best quotes  Wolfgang Puck has been seen many times  by customers but never in the light  Terry Dunham remembers well one evening  he entered one of pucks new restaurants  in Las Vegas the Californian Pizza  Kitchen at the MGM Grand Hotel as dalam  tells the story he walked in and sat  down only to see puck through the open  kitchen he was surprised to see him  there at all but what surprised him more  was puck came out and took his order  then proceeded to make the pizza he  ordered himself  Belem stated that he could see puck toss  the dough put the ingredients on the  pizza and then place it in the oven  according to dalam he thought maybe this  was a dream and said he smiled  each time he watched puck sampling each  one of the raw ingredients before he  placed them on delivers pizza here was a  man worth around 500 million dollars  when the host of restaurants around the  country is the most famous chef in the  world is the main caterer at the  Governor's Ball the Academy Awards for  the past 15 years but took the time to  make one person of Pizza delhomme States  Puck brought out the pizza and it was  the best he ever had  thank you for joining me for another  edition model and a masters if you liked  the video and you want to see more  please give it a thumbs up below I'd  also love to hear what you have to think  if you own leave a comment under the  video and you will see you on the next  episode  you
 

